{"step_index":704,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-16T20:12:07Z","input_tokens":3003,"cache_read_tokens":30909,"output_tokens":1572,"content":"Graphs **3**, **4**, and **5** have been generated in **vector PDF** (for LaTeX inclusion) and **high-resolution PNG** (300 DPI).\n\n---\n\n### **Graph 3: Net Container Memory Scaling (Alpine vs. Ubuntu Heavy)**\n* **Local files:** [`graph3_memory_scaling.pdf`](file:///home/davidel/.gemini/antigravity/brain/335ea41a-df46-4ffa-bb4c-eefc5a5248cd/scratch/thesis_figures/graph3_memory_scaling.pdf) | [`graph3_memory_scaling.png`](file:///home/davidel/.gemini/antigravity/brain/335ea41a-df46-4ffa-bb4c-eefc5a5248cd/scratch/thesis_figures/graph3_memory_scaling.png)\n* **Remote path:** `/home/debian/bluectfd/thesis_figures/graph3_memory_scaling.pdf`\n\n```\nRAM Delta (MB) = Total RAM Used - ZFS ARC Cache - Host Idle Baseline\n```\n* **Alpine:** Linear slope of **$14.9\\text{ MB} / \\text{container}$** ($+1,533\\text{ MB}$ net at 100 concurrent containers).\n* **Ubuntu Heavy:** Linear slope of **$52.7\\text{ MB} / \\text{container}$** ($+5,247\\text{ MB}$ net at 100 concurrent containers with systemd, PostgreSQL, and Nginx idling).\n* **Thesis Takeaway:** Proves strict $O(N)$ linear memory scaling with zero memory leaks. Even at peak scale ($100$ concurrent instances), Ubuntu Heavy consumes only **$9.23\\text{ GiB}$** on a $16\\text{ GiB}$ host with $0\\text{ MB}$ swap paging.\n\n---\n\n### **Graph 4: Host Lifecycle Telemetry Timeline (Tier $M=10, N=5$ — 100 Containers)**\n* **Local files:** [`graph4_lifecycle_timeline.pdf`](file:///home/davidel/.gemini/antigravity/brain/335ea41a-df46-4ffa-bb4c-eefc5a5248cd/scratch/thesis_figures/graph4_lifecycle_timeline.pdf) | [`graph4_lifecycle_timeline.png`](file:///home/davidel/.gemini/antigravity/brain/335ea41a-df46-4ffa-bb4c-eefc5a5248cd/scratch/thesis_figures/graph4_lifecycle_timeline.png)\n* **Remote path:** `/home/debian/bluectfd/thesis_figures/graph4_lifecycle_timeline.pdf`\n\n* **Telemetry:** 100ms continuous sampling across 225 seconds of execution with dual y-axes (CPU % across 8 cores and Net Container RAM Delta).\n* **Phases Tracked:**\n  1. *Provision Teams* ($0 \\to 4\\text{s}$): Lightweight OVN switch creation.\n  2. *Deploy Challenges* ($4 \\to 105\\text{s}$): RAM ramps steadily to $+2,600\\text{ MB}$ as 50 live containers boot.\n  3. *Verify Setup* ($105 \\to 181\\text{s}$): CoW clones launch in parallel bursts; RAM peaks at **$+5,247\\text{ MB}$** when all 100 containers are live simultaneously.\n  4. *Verify Cleanup & Teardown* ($181 \\to 225\\text{s}$): RAM collapses symmetrically back to baseline $+0\\text{ MB}$.\n* **Thesis Takeaway:** Demonstrates system stability under maximum load: CPU load averages $19.1\\%$ without saturation spikes, and memory deallocation is instantaneous and complete upon verification teardown.\n\n---\n\n### **Graph 5: Host CPU Utilization & I/O Wait Across Lifecycle Barriers**\n* **Local files:** [`graph5_step_cpu_iowait.pdf`](file:///home/davidel/.gemini/antigravity/brain/335ea41a-df46-4ffa-bb4c-eefc5a5248cd/scratch/thesis_figures/graph5_step_cpu_iowait.pdf) | [`graph5_step_cpu_iowait.png`](file:///home/davidel/.gemini/antigravity/brain/335ea41a-df46-4ffa-bb4c-eefc5a5248cd/scratch/thesis_figures/graph5_step_cpu_iowait.png)\n* **Remote path:** `/home/debian/bluectfd/thesis_figures/graph5_step_cpu_iowait.pdf`\n\n* **Barrier Breakdown:**\n  * **CPU Utilization:** Ranges from $6.2\\%$ to $20.9\\%$ across all steps. Active CPU is never the bottleneck.\n  * **I/O Wait:** Peaks during *Verify Setup* ($36.4\\%$ Alpine, $44.1\\%$ Ubuntu) and *Teardown Machines* ($40.8\\%$ Alpine, $43.7\\%$ Ubuntu).\n* **Thesis Takeaway:** Confirms that parallel container lifecycles on a single NVMe drive are **I/O-bound rather than compute-bound**, justifying the architectural choice of ZFS Copy-on-Write snapshots to eliminate disk write bottlenecks during verification runs.\n\n---\n\n### **Complete Thesis Figures Suite Summary**\n| Figure | File | Key Insight |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **1** | `graph1_cow_vs_deploy.pdf` | **$3.44\\times - 3.60\\times$ CoW speedup** over cold deployment at scale |\n| **2** | `graph2_microphase_breakdown.pdf` | CoW clone time stays flat while deploy creation grows |\n| **3** | `graph3_memory_scaling.pdf` | Strict linear density: $14.9\\text{ MB}$ (Alpine) vs. $52.7\\text{ MB}$ (Ubuntu) |\n| **4** | `graph4_lifecycle_timeline.pdf` | Dual-axis telemetry showing 100 simultaneous containers at rest |\n| **5** | `graph5_step_cpu_iowait.pdf` | I/O-bound bottleneck confirmation ($<21\\%$ CPU, up to $44\\%$ I/O wait) |"}
