{"step_index":712,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-16T22:06:14Z","input_tokens":2439,"cache_read_tokens":44445,"output_tokens":774,"content":"I have synthesized all empirical experiments, telemetry data, hardware benchmarks, and architectural findings into a complete, academic-grade thesis evaluation chapter.\n\nThe full chapter has been saved to:\n* **Local Artifact:** [`thesis_evaluation_chapter.md`](file:///home/davidel/.gemini/antigravity/brain/335ea41a-df46-4ffa-bb4c-eefc5a5248cd/thesis_evaluation_chapter.md)\n* **Remote Path:** `/home/debian/bluectfd/thesis_evaluation_chapter.md`\n\n### **Summary of Chapter Sections**\n1. **Abstract & Introduction:** Motivation, trade-offs between hypervisors and shared namespaces, and the 5 central research questions (RQ1–RQ5).\n2. **Experimental Methodology & Infrastructure:**\n   * Testbed hardware specifications (8 cores, $15.6\\text{ GiB}$ RAM, NVMe ZFS).\n   * Workload characterization: Alpine ($3.21\\text{ MiB}$) vs. Ubuntu Heavy ($1.5\\text{ GiB}$, `systemd`, PostgreSQL 16, Nginx).\n   * Subprocess telemetry engine formulation isolating net container RAM from ZFS ARC cache.\n   * Six-barrier synchronization protocol ($2 \\times M \\times N$ concurrency model).\n3. **Empirical Results & Discussion:**\n   * **CoW Speedup & Scale Invariance:** $3.44\\times - 3.60\\times$ speedup at scale; proof of $O(1)$ block-pointer metadata cloning ($0.46\\text{s}$ vs $0.49\\text{s}$ across a $460\\times$ image size disparity).\n   * **Microphase Decomposition:** Stacked analysis of creation vs. network vs. boot latencies.\n   * **Linear Memory Density:** Empirical models ($14.9\\text{ MB/ct}$ Alpine, $52.7\\text{ MB/ct}$ Ubuntu), $9.23\\text{ GiB}$ peak host memory, $0\\text{ MB}$ swap paging.\n   * **Telemetry & Elasticity:** 225s timeline proving instantaneous and complete deallocation.\n   * **Host Bottlenecks:** CPU ($<21\\%$) vs. Storage I/O Wait (up to $44.1\\%$), confirming orchestration is I/O-bound.\n4. **Architectural Challenges & Solutions:** OVN dynamic address pool lock contention analysis and static lease allocation fix.\n5. **Conclusions & Contribution Matrix:** Academic takeaway summary.\n\n---\n\n### **Decisions & Next Steps for Your Thesis**\n1. **LaTeX Conversion:** Would you like this chapter converted directly into ready-to-compile `.tex` files with formatted `table` and `figure` environments?\n2. **Additional Figures:** Would you like to generate the **Amortized Per-Container Latency** or **Hysteresis Elasticity Loop** graphs discussed earlier to include as supplementary figures?"}
